<title>USA: Nematron launches real-time software.</title>
<headline>Nematron launches real-time software.</headline>
<dateline>ANN ARBOR, Mich. 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nematron Corp said Monday it launched a software product called Hyperkernel, which allows Microsoft Windows NT to be used as a real-time operating system.</p>
<p>Real-time operating systems are used for very specialized applications such as machine control and robots. The real-time operating system market is expected to reach $900 million by 1998, the company said.</p>
<p>Nematron said it will license the technology through a subsidiary, Imagination Systems, which it plans to form.</p>
<p>Previously Windows did not provide a real-time operating system for these types of applications.</p>
<p>--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
